{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_delta","contentIndex":1,"delta":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/user/work/delegate-10-resume-cancel && git branch --show-current && git diff --stat && git add src/cli.rs src/status_record.rs src/types.rs src/job_registry.rs tests/cli_e2e.rs && git commit -m \\\"feat: delegate resume and cancel (#10)\\n\\nresume reads a job record, reuses model/cwd/capability/gate/tool-idle\\nwindow plus backend session, applies model/capability/gate overrides,\\nand starts a new job through run's shared launch path. A cross-backend\\nmodel override exits 2. The new record carries resumedFrom; the old\\nrecord gains supersededBy once the new job is spawned. Resume on a\\nRUNNING job, a record with no session id, an unknown id, or an empty\\nprompt exits 2; a read-write resume into a locked cwd is BUSY (exit 3).\\n\\ncancel SIGTERMs the supervisor's process group and the supervisor\\ntranslates that into registry.cancel (SIGTERM to the agent's own group,\\nCANCELLED record). After 5s without a terminal record, cancel SIGKILLs\\nboth groups and writes the CANCELLED record itself. Cancelling a\\nterminal job prints its record and exits 0; an unknown id exits 2.\\n\\nThe supervisor's cancel path uses a SIGTERM handler plus self-pipe\\nrather than a blocked mask, so the agent child never inherits a blocked\\nSIGTERM. Kill finalization now marks the result itself CANCELLED or\\nSTALLED to match the record status.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Muse Spark 1.3 <noreply@opencode.ai>\\\" && git log --oneline -2 && git status --short\""}}
