dded `CANCELLED`/`STALLED` to `RunStatus` so the result status can match the record status) and `src/job_registry.rs` (kill finalization now sets `out.status` from the termination instead of leaving the derived `ERROR`).\n\nFriction:\n- The brief's suggested `pthread_sigmask` + `sigwait` would leave SIGTERM blocked in the forked agent child, making it unkillable — used a handler + self-pipe instead (same pattern as `index.rs`), worth stating in the ticket.\n- The literal cancel line (`result.status: CANCELLED`) was unrepresentable — `RunStatus` had no such variant — so the fence had to stretch to `types.rs`/`job_registry.rs`; the spec's \"Check these against what your code actually writes\" is what caught it.\n- `resume --gate` with an empty stored gate plus `--gate \"\"` is indistinguishable from \"no override\", so clearing a gate on resume is impossible — fine for now, but the flag can't express it.\n\nSTATUS: DONE","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_01a0f704b71e7064936fce49c12b0f92\"}"}],"api":"openai-responses","provider":"opencode-go","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","usage":{"input":196,"output":435,"cacheRead":125297,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":24,"totalTokens":125928,"cost":{"input":0.000019600000000000002,"output":0.00008700000000000001,"cacheRead":0.00025059400000000003,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.000357194}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1790850674846,"responseId":"resp_6abe36742a32172422f045db","rawStopReason":"completed","thinkingLevel":"high"}],"willRetry":false}
